  "question": {
    "text": "A hydrogen atom moving at speed <math><mi>v</mi></math> collides with another hydrogen atom kept at rest. Find the minimum value of <math><mi>v</mi></math> for which one of the atoms may get ionised. The mass of a hydrogen atom <math><mo>=</mo><mn>1.67</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27&nbsp;</mn></mrow></msup><mi>kg</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Assume completely inelastic collision."
  },
